## DockingService

**Namespace**: `Cyrena.Services`  
**Assembly**: `Cyrena.Components.Runtime`  
**Implements**: `IDockingService`

### Purpose
Manages docked panel requests in the UI. Allows kernel-aware components to be docked as panels with lifecycle management. Uses an internal `EventPipeline` for pub/sub communication.

### Implementation

```csharp
internal class DockingService : IDockingService
{
    private readonly DockingPipeline _pipe;

    public DockingService()
    {
        _pipe = new DockingPipeline();
    }

    public void Dock<TKernelComponent>(string title, Action onClose) 
        where TKernelComponent : KernelComponentBase
    {
        var r = new IDockingService.DockRequest(typeof(TKernelComponent), title, onClose);
        _pipe.InvokeDockingRequest(r);
    }

    public IDisposable OnDockRequest(Action<IDockingService.DockRequest> callback) 
        => _pipe.WatchRequest(callback);
}
```

### DockingPipeline

```csharp
internal class DockingPipeline : EventPipeline
{
    public IDisposable WatchRequest(Action<IDockingService.DockRequest> cb) 
        => this.ConfigurePipe("dock", cb);

    public void InvokeDockingRequest(IDockingService.DockRequest r) 
        => this.InvokePipeline("dock", r);
}
```

### Methods

| Method | Signature | Description |
|--------|-----------|-------------|
| `Dock` | `void Dock<TKernelComponent>(string title, Action onClose)` | Creates a dock request for a kernel component type |
| `OnDockRequest` | `IDisposable OnDockRequest(Action<IDockingService.DockRequest> callback)` | Subscribes to dock requests with automatic cleanup |

### DockRequest Model

```csharp
public record DockRequest(Type ComponentType, string Title, Action OnClose);
```

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `ComponentType` | `Type` | The `KernelComponentBase` derived type to dock |
| `Title` | `string` | Panel title displayed in the UI |
| `OnClose` | `Action` | Callback invoked when the panel is closed |

### Architecture

The service uses a custom `EventPipeline` (from Cyrena.Core) for pub/sub:
- **Publisher**: Any code calling `Dock<T>()` creates and publishes a `DockRequest`
- **Subscriber**: UI components call `OnDockRequest()` to receive dock requests and render panels
- **Cleanup**: Subscriptions return `IDisposable` for automatic cleanup

### Thread Safety

The `EventPipeline` base class handles subscriber cleanup automatically when subscribers are disposed. The `DockingPipeline` uses the pipeline's built-in locking for thread-safe invocation.

